02"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-12T04:56:10-07:00","id":1260268,"title":"","content":"That's tricky because before the beyond existed the wyld was trying to encompass all weirdness, I think you need to define what the wyld is to first even if that contradicts canon sources.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-12T07:19:24-07:00","id":1260285,"title":"","content":"that could be interesting, under normal circumstances the possessed seems like any other person, maybe a little odd sure but well within what could be called normal. now under stressful situations I could see some body horror/mutations that comes along the way the anime parasyte","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-12T10:24:55-07:00","id":1260308,"title":"","content":"Well what's the 3rd circle that's doing the possession? That helps narrow things down a bit since there's a difference in themes represented by a third circle. I think one of Kimberry's thirds is basically an insanely chaotic blood red moon, and another is a more humanoid appearing general who can erode fortress walls by glaring at them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-12T12:52:27-07:00","id":1260331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1260104-beyond-or-wyld?p=1260308#post1260308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well what's the 3rd circle that's doing the possession? That helps narrow things down a bit since there's a difference in themes represented by a third circle. I think one of Kimberry's thirds is basically an insanely chaotic blood red moon, and another is a more humanoid appearing general who can erode fortress walls by glaring at them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a portion of the Unfettered Heart actually!<br /> ...Oramus has exactly 2 detailed 3rd circles (Skittering Jungle and the one who mutates people by passing by them). Which...maybe should have been chosen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-12T19:55:24-07:00","id":1260386,"title":"","content":"Don't know hoow much this has been adressed, but a major element of Oramus and its souls seems to be the subject of <i><b>contradictions</b></i>, things that show themselves to be the &quot;opposite&quot; of what they are &quot;supposed&quot; to, such as a jungle that moves, because its &quot;trees&quot; are actually metal insects that play at immobility to catch prey, seeming cllockwork beings with bowels of metal and dark oily blood and ichors, a multitude that yet is one unique being.<br /> <br /> What if when, it comes to a soul of Oramus', the <i>possessed</i> shapes the possession? The mortal invites the demon in, so it may shape into reality insane dreams beyond the reach of the possessed? Just a funny rambling thought of mine, &quot;<i>In Oramus' possession, demon is taken over by <b>you</b>.</i>&quot;, so to speak.<br /> <br /> But a little more into the topic, could this 2e blurb related to Benezet, the Gardener of Identities, be of interest/relevance to the subject?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoCD:Malfeas, pg.118</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When an artist or craftsman creates something truly unique, something never seen in Creation, Benezet may emerge from the demon prison without sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyway Benezet i guess sounds like the go-to demon for whatever twisted ideas and imagery the OP might have in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-13-2018, 12:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}